  "abstract": "A falsifiable jamming→unjamming mechanism for a rapid phase of continental break-up, with the Atlantic as test case. An antipodal rupture opens a pressure-deficit void whose suction, plus unjamming-liquefaction friction collapse (μ_eff ≈ 2.2×10⁻³, no melt), can drive runaway sliding. 35 pre-registered predictions with PASS/HOLD/FAIL gates; four bounded HOLDs; a chronology firewall that concedes the U–Pb break-up ages and stays chronology-agnostic.",
